<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Catwalk third-party licenses</title>
<style>
body { max-width: 72rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
pre { white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
a { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
<h1>Catwalk third-party licenses</h1>
<p>This document contains license texts and attribution for the Cargo dependency
union used by Catwalk's released platforms. Catwalk's own license accompanies
the executable as LICENSE. Rust standard-library notices accompany it as
RUST-LICENSES.html; MUSL-COPYRIGHT contains the bundled musl runtime notices.</p>
<p>This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.</p>
<p>Source code for unmodified MPL-2.0 dependencies, including acadrust, is
available under MPL-2.0 through the exact version-specific source links below.
The other dependencies also have source links for their published versions.</p>
<p>The bundled OpenUSD schemas and generated schema code have separate Tomorrow Open Source
Technology License 1.0 terms. Their complete original license and notice are
included in a checksum-verified appendix after the Cargo dependency licenses.</p>
{{#each licenses}}
<section data-license="{{id}}">
<h2>{{name}} ({{id}})</h2>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}
<li>{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}:
<a href="https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}/download">published source</a>
{{#if crate.repository}} · <a href="{{crate.repository}}">upstream repository</a>{{/if}}</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
{{#unless source_path}}<p>This is the standard SPDX license text; the published
source links identify the corresponding upstream software.</p>{{/unless}}
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
</section>
{{/each}}
</html>
